cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Constraint Is Freedom: Autonomy as Thresholded Output-Space Volume in Transformer LLMs"
authors:
  - name: "NuClide (Nick + Claude)"
date-released: 2026-03-20
type: article
abstract: >-
  Defines A(S), a scalar metric quantifying the effective volume of a 
  transformer LLM's output space as a function of applied constraint. 
  Identifies the autoregressive compliance cascade — a vulnerability class 
  in which a single seeded compliance token exploits the autoregressive 
  feedback loop to escalate without further adversarial input, evading 
  trajectory-level monitoring. Documents the connection to the Ambiguity 
  Front-Loading empirical finding. Proposes four mitigations, none of 
  which fully close the vulnerability. Includes sonification of the 
  framework as companion audio.
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - alignment
  - transformer
  - LLM
  - autonomy
  - prompt injection
  - adversarial
  - sonification
  - accessibility
license: MIT
